Cache

Many kinds exist.

React Query Cache

Stores API responses on the frontend.

⸻

Redis Cache

Stores data to avoid hitting the database repeatedly.

⸻

Prompt Cache

Some providers reuse repeated prompt prefixes internally to reduce latency and cost for identical prompt segments. This is provider-specific.

⸻

KV Cache

One of the biggest optimizations inside LLM inference.

The model remembers intermediate computations while generating tokens, so it doesn’t recompute everything for every new output token.

We’ll study KV Cache later because it’s an inference optimization rather than a context-management concept.